# Applies when this checkout is used as a Docker build context -- see the
# "patient-management-local" additional build context in
# openmrs-distro-referenceapplication/frontend/Dockerfile, which lets the distro
# build this repo from a local checkout instead of cloning it from GitHub.
#
# The point is to make the copied context look like a fresh `git clone`: the
# Dockerfile runs `yarn install` and `yarn build` itself, so a host-built
# node_modules is not just a huge pointless transfer, it can leak a
# host-platform install into the image. The patterns below mirror .gitignore.
#
# IMPORTANT: .yarn/releases must NOT be excluded -- .yarnrc.yml sets
# `yarnPath: .yarn/releases/yarn-4.10.3.cjs`, so dropping it breaks `yarn install`
# inside the container. Only .yarn/cache (gitignored, re-fetched on install) and
# the install-state are excluded.

# Dependencies -- reinstalled in the container. `**/` is required: a bare
# `node_modules` would only match the root one, leaving packages/*/node_modules.
**/node_modules

# Build output -- rebuilt in the container
**/dist
**/.turbo
**/*.tgz
**/coverage
**/.nyc_output
**/.eslintcache

# Yarn state -- keep .yarn/releases (see note above)
.yarn/cache
.yarn/install-state.gz

# Test artefacts
**/test-results
**/playwright-report
**/playwright/.cache

# Local / editor cruft
.env
.idea
.vscode
**/.DS_Store
**/*.log
